  "claims": [
    "Four actual local wire/fusion squares extend to arbitrary eighteen-law proof tracks, including inverses, without new higher generators.",
    "Pairing the left and right comparisons moves both component tracks across sequential or tensor fusion. These comparisons have empty support; any single circuit placement adds exactly its own requirements.",
    "Applying the actual component normalization tracks returns comparisons with exactly the existing WirePass witness on the source.",
    "For sequential composition, the component-normalization Cell followed by the existing canonical seqWire Cell equals the actual whole-wire normalizeCell. Equality transports are proved explicitly; the corresponding emitted union proof tracks are equal.",
    "This proof-track equality closes the sequential fusion/wire-pass higher square using the previously defined canonical fusion residual, with empty support. No arbitrary parallel-path generator, extra local root or backtracking residual is introduced.",
    "The actual sequential square in a circuit placement has exactly the placement requirements. Repair yields a correlated joint-law equality from the original sequential wire circuit to the normalized fused circuit in one updated checked shared-state MAC model."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Tensor fusion has the full component-track exchange, but no completed square with the canonical whole-wire normalization path.",
    "Pure-wire higher coherence, all mixed root overlaps and finite complete local basis are not proved.",
    "The new square is in the existing richer presented basis of the MAC structural/fusion/wire example. It is not yet inserted into the generic PathResidual contextual contract, which still targets Exchange homotopies.",
    "The joint-law theorem applies to the original circuit and the normalized fused circuit inside the updated model, not two arbitrary model revisions.",
    "No new code-changing reduction, runtime guarantee, key-generation execution or MAC advantage bound is claimed.",
    "No encoded-certificate, checker-time or fair shared-proof cost advantage is established.",
    "Novelty remains unconfirmed. This is an implementation/proof-construction advance, not a claim that generic naturality is new. No new external primary sources or independent review in this stage."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Construct the pure-wire higher comparison tensorInner(normalize(p),normalize(q));wireTrack(tensorWire(p,q)) => normalize(tensor(p,q)) using actual local diagrams. Endpoint equality is insufficient.",
    "Generalize the path-valued contextual compatibility contract to the existing richer contextual higher presentation, then instantiate the completed sequential root.",
    "Classify and resolve the remaining pure/mixed root overlaps and establish finite local-basis coverage.",
    "Preserve original full objective: computational reductions/losses/resources, continuous execution through oracle internals/keygen, fair total-cost comparison and theorem-level novelty assessment."
  ],
